SOLUTION
Step 1: Create the Job template file
Create /home/thor/countdown-datacenter-t3q2.yml with the following content:

yaml
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: countdown-datacenter-t3q2
spec:
  template:
    metadata:
      name: countdown-datacenter-t3q2
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: container-countdown-datacenter-t3q2
          image: debian:latest
          command: ["sleep", "5"]
      restartPolicy: Never
Create it with a heredoc:

bash
cat <<'EOF' > /home/thor/countdown-datacenter-t3q2.yml
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: Job
metadata:
  name: countdown-datacenter-t3q2
spec:
  template:
    metadata:
      name: countdown-datacenter-t3q2
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: container-countdown-datacenter-t3q2
          image: debian:latest
          command: ["sleep", "5"]
      restartPolicy: Never
EOF
⚠️ Key points:

apiVersion: batch/v1 — Jobs live under batch, not apps or core v1.

spec.template.metadata.name — the pod template name, as required.

Container name is exactly container-countdown-datacenter-t3q2.

restartPolicy: Never — required for Jobs. If omitted, it defaults to Always, which is rejected by the API server for a Job (spec.template.spec.restartPolicy: Unsupported value: "Always": supported values: "OnFailure", "Never").

Step 2: Apply the Job
bash
kubectl apply -f /home/thor/countdown-datacenter-t3q2.yml
Expected output:

text
job.batch/countdown-datacenter-t3q2 created
