Notes / troubleshooting
If you previously created the Job incorrectly (e.g., missing restartPolicy: Never), Jobs are mostly immutable — you cannot patch restartPolicy in place. Delete and recreate:

bash
kubectl delete job countdown-datacenter-t3q2
kubectl apply -f /home/thor/countdown-datacenter-t3q2.yml
Unsupported value: "Always" error — this is exactly what happens when restartPolicy is omitted; the default Always is invalid for Jobs. Add restartPolicy: Never.

ImagePullBackOff — node can't pull debian:latest; check kubectl describe pod <pod-name>.

Command format — command: ["sleep", "5"] is the exec-form array, which is the safest YAML form. If you write command: sleep 5 as a string, it won't run as expected (Kubernetes would try to execute a binary literally named sleep 5). If you need a shell, use command: ["/bin/sh", "-c", "sleep 5"].

Pod stuck in Running — with sleep 5 it should finish within ~5s. If it lingers, check kubectl logs <pod-name> and kubectl describe pod <pod-name>.

-- for viewing the completed pod's details — a completed Job pod shows STATUS: Completed; that's normal and satisfies "job ran successfully."
